---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Graham Lyle | Launch Baseball">
  <main>
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="eyebrow">Co-Founder</p>
        <h1>Graham Lyle</h1>
        <p class="focus">Hitting • Middle Infield</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="paper">
      <div class="container profile-grid">
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">Why I Coach</p>

          <p class="lead">
            My first season coaching high school baseball changed the way I looked at hitting.
          </p>

          <p>I expected to teach effort.</p>

          <p>I expected to teach competition.</p>

          <p>I expected to help players improve.</p>

          <p>What I didn't expect was how differently players had been taught.</p>

          <p>Some had a strong foundation.</p>

          <p>Some had almost no foundation at all.</p>

          <p>Others had spent years trying to build on ideas that simply weren't helping them.</p>

          <p>I realized the biggest gap wasn't effort.</p>

          <p><strong>It was understanding.</strong></p>

          <p>That's when Launch Baseball began.</p>

          <p>
            I wanted to build a system that organized the movement principles shared by successful hitters into something players could understand, coaches could teach, and parents could follow.
          </p>

          <p>
            Because every player deserves to understand what they're doing and why they're doing it.
          </p>

          <hr />

          <h2>What I Believe</h2>

          <p>
            I don't believe every player should look the same. I do believe successful hitters share common movement principles.
          </p>

          <p>
            My job is not to make every player copy someone else's swing. My job is to help each player understand those principles and apply them to their own game.
          </p>

          <h2>My Goal</h2>

          <p>
            I don't want players to depend on me. I want them to leave every lesson understanding their swing better than when they arrived.
          </p>

          <p><strong>Understanding creates independence.</strong></p>
        </article>

        <aside>
          <p class="aside-label">Areas of Focus</p>
          <p>Hitting</p>
          <p>Middle Infield</p>

          <div class="quote">
            Every player deserves to understand what they're doing and why they're doing it.
          </div>

          <a class="text-link" href="/assessment">Book a Launch Assessment →</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .hero {
      padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 78% 25%, rgba(211,41,47,.23), transparent 28%),
        linear-gradient(135deg, var(--navy), var(--navy-2));
    }
    h1 {
      margin: .4rem 0 .7rem;
      font-size: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 8rem);
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .focus {
      color: #bcc7d1;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-weight: 900;
      letter-spacing: .1em;
    }
    .paper {
      padding: 7rem 0;
      background: var(--paper);
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .profile-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 310px;
      gap: 5rem;
      align-items: start;
    }
    article {
      max-width: 760px;
    }
    article p {
      color: #46525d;
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
    article .lead {
      color: var(--ink);
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1.12;
    }
    article strong { color: var(--ink); }
    article hr {
      margin: 4rem 0;
      border: 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
    }
    h2 {
      margin: 3rem 0 .8rem;
      font-size: 2.1rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: 110px;
      padding: 1.5rem;
      background: white;
      border-left: 5px solid var(--red);
    }
    aside p { color: #46525d; }
    .aside-label {
      color: var(--red);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .12em;
      font-size: .72rem;
      font-weight: 950;
    }
    .quote {
      margin: 1.8rem 0;
      padding-top: 1.4rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--paper-line);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 900;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }
    @media (max-width: 800px) {
      .profile-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      aside { position: static; }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
